1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Eugene R. "Gene" Hagen, 63, Grand Forks, ND, died Tuesday, February 7, 2006, in Valley Eldercare Center after a long battle and complications with diabetes.
2 CONT
2 CONT Eugene Rodney Hagen was born March 6, 1942, the son of Milford and Bertha (Knutson) Hagen in Roseau, MN. He attended school in Roseau until his family moved to East Grand Forks, MN in 1956.
2 CONT
2 CONT He worked on area farms and was well known as a musician and band leader. He performed around the area during the 60's, 70's and 80's in a band call the "Country Travelers" and later led the band known as "The Knightmen". He was e
2 CONC mployed in the building maintenance departments of the University of North Dakota and later, North Dakota State University, retiring from there in 1995. He married Elsie Lund on June 23, 1979 in Grand Forks. He enjoyed playing gui
2 CONC tar with friends and fishing.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is survived by his wife, Elsie; daughters, Kristy Hagen, Madison, WI, Sheila (Steve) Romero and Christie (Tony) Krewson both of Grand Forks, ND, Jolene (Paul) Dybas, Pass Christian, MS; sons, Joey Hagen and Michael Gilchrist bo
2 CONC th of Madison, WI and Scott (Deb) Lund, Colorado Springs, CO; 12 grandchildren; sisters, Mertrice (Kenneth) Anderson and MaryLou (Vince) Liddy both of Grand Forks, ND; a brother, Jerry (Patti) Hagen, Fargo, ND, many nieces and nep
2 CONC hews and his best buddy, Regis.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was preceded in death by a grandchild, Angel Love Lund and his parents.
