1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Reference: [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:Q23M-7VLR FamilySearch Record] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Nov 17 2019, 17:31:37 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT Lewis Edward Drehman, 92, of Bartlesville, died at 3:02 A.M. on Monday, January 5, 2015 at the Jane Phillips Medical Center. Mr. Drehman was born in Chicago, Illinois on January 6, 1922 to Marie Elvira (Fuller) and Edward Hugo Dre
2 CONC hmann. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He grew up and received his education in Chicago and earned his Bachelor’s Degree in Chemical Engineering from the University of Chicago. He came to Bartlesville and was employed with Phillips Petroleum Company on April 1, 1942 an
2 CONC d during his career with Phillips he was awarded 40 patents. Mr. Drehman retired on August 1, 1985. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Drehman was married to Norma Lee Sushnik on April 15, 1945 in Bartlesville. They made their home in Bartlesville their entire married life and Mrs. Drehman preceded him in death on May 28, 1981. Mr. Drehman had been a long tim
2 CONC e member of the Adams Golf Club , was active in bowling for many years and was still active in a bowling league at the time of his death. In past years he had also been active in playing in and judging chess tournaments. He was a 
2 CONC member of the First Presbyterian Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Dehman is survived by a son, Ken Drehman and wife Joyce of Bartlesville, one daughter, Judy Green and husband John of Nowata, four grandchildren, Jenni Green Griggs, Cory Green, Tracy Rae Packard King and Amanda Gail Packard C
2 CONC agle, three great grandchildren, Nicholas James Cagle, Ttacy Gail Cagle and Phoebe Ray King, and two great great grandchildren, Trent James Cagle and Ryker Lee Griggs. In addition to his wife, Mr. Drehman was preceded in death by 
2 CONC his parents.
2 CONT
2 CONT Memorial services for Mr. Drehman will be held at 2 P.M. on Wednesday, January 7, 2015 in the Stumpff Funeral Home Chapel with Rev. Charles McKnight officiating.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/140993631 Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Nov 17 2019, 17:37:12 UTC''
