1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Reference: [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:XRP9-MH3 FamilySearch Record] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 15 2019, 0:22:12 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT Catharine Hazelwood, 96  Catharine Ries Meyer Hazelwood of West Bend died Tuesday, Oct. 12 at St. Joseph’s Community hospital at the age of 96.  She was born Oct. 31, 1902 in Milwaukee to the late Alfred L. and Belle (nee Ogden) R
2 CONC ies.  When she was in high school, the family moved to Brooklyn, N.Y. where she married Alfred H. Meyer on April 28, 1926.  The family summered at Big Cedar Lake from 1936 until making their permanent home in 1965 when they moved 
2 CONC to West Bend.  Her husband predeceased in 1978.  After her marriage to Preston Hazelwood in 1989 in West Bend, the couple moved to Setauket, N.Y. until his death in 1993 when she returned to West Bend.  Catharine was a member of t
2 CONC he Cedar Lake Yacht Club and served as president of the women’s auxiliary the Joseph Marest Chapter of D.A.R., St. Joseph’s Community Hospital Auxiliary and St. James Episcopal Church.  Survivors include one son, Robert A. (Patric
2 CONC ia) Meyer of West Bend; a step-daughter, Gail Hazelwood of Minneapolis, four grandchildren, Laurie (Thomas) Wagner, Robert O. (Sandra) Meyer, both of West Bend, James A. (Gayle) Meyer of Mequon and Ann (Kenneth) Carrano of Gurney,
2 CONC  Ill; six great-grandchildren, Kelly and Kara Wagner, Ben and Adam Meyer, Christopher and Elizabeth Carrano; three step-great-grandchildren, Missy, Andrew and Eric Sawyer; one brother, Howard A. (Carol) Ries of Wilton, Conn.; othe
2 CONC r relatives and friends.  Funeral services will be held Friday at 12 noon at St. James Episcopal Church with Father R. Michael Darrow officiating.  Burial will follow at Forest Home Cemetery, Milwaukee.  Visitation at the church w
2 CONC ill be from 10 a.m. Friday until the time of services.  In lieu of flowers, memorials may be given to St. James Episcopal Church, the Washington County Historical Society or the charity of the donor’s choice.  The Schmidt Funeral 
2 CONC Home is serving the family.
