1 NAME Robert A. /Meyer/
2 GIVN Robert A.
2 SURN Meyer
2 _MARNM Meyer
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 16 APR 1928
2 ADDR
3 CITY Brooklyn
3 STAE NY
3 CTRY United States
1 BURI
2 DATE AFT 14 APR 2013
2 PLAC Washington County Memorial Park, West Bend, Washington County, Wisconsin, USA
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 14 APR 2013
2 PLAC West Bend, Washington County, Wisconsin, USA
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Robert A. Meyer, 84, of West Bend died on Sunday, April 14, 2013, at the Lighthouse of West Bend. He was born on April 16, 1928, in Brooklyn, N.Y. to the late Alfred and Catharine (nee Ries) Meyer.
2 CONT
2 CONT He attended school in Brooklyn and graduated from Brooklyn Technical High School. He then went on to graduate from Stevens Institute of Technology in Hoboken, N.J., where he played lacrosse and sailed.
2 CONT
2 CONT For two years during the Korean Conflict, he served with the United States Army. Following his discharge, he moved to Wisconsin where he had spent many summers at Big Cedar Lake. He then earned his master's degree in engineering f
2 CONC rom the University of Wisconsin-Madison and became a professional engineer (P.E.) in Wisconsin.
2 CONT
2 CONT On May 7, 1955, he was united in marriage to Patricia A. Kaempfer at Trinity Lutheran Church in West Bend.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bob worked at Amity Leather Products and later for Will Ross Inc. He then became employed at Children's Hospital of Wisconsin as a facilities engineer, from where he retired.
2 CONT
2 CONT As an active resident of the community, he was a member and past president of the West Bend Jaycees, the West Bend Noon Kiwanis Club and the Washington County Historical Society, member and past commodore of the Cedar Lake Yacht C
2 CONC lub, and member and past commodore of the Military Order of the Loyal Legion of the United States-Wisconsin Commandery. Additional memberships include the West Bend Masonic Lodge 138 F. and A. M. (Free and Accepted Masons), Scotti
2 CONC sh Rite-Valley of Milwaukee and Tripoli Shrine Temple AAOMS (Ancient Arabic Order of the Mystic Shrine). He also served on the Washington County Landmarks Commission. In addition to coaching Little League baseball in West Bend, he
2 CONC  bowled, played basketball and golfed in his younger years.
2 CONT
2 CONT As a member of St. James Episcopal Church, he participated in many aspects of the parish and was a lay reader.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include his wife Pat; four children Laurie (Tom) Wagner of West Bend, Bob (Sandra) of West Bend, James (Gayle) of Mequon and Ann (Ken) Carrano of Gurnee, Ill.; six grandchildren Kelly (Chris) Lang, Kara (Corey) Petzold, 
2 CONC Ben and Adam Meyer and Christopher and Elizabeth Carrano; two great-grandchildren Evan Lang and Grace Petzold; three step grandchildren Melissa (Nick) Mueller, Andrew (Anna) Sawyer and Eric Sawyer; one step-great-grandson Noah Mue
2 CONC ller; one brother-in-law Robert (Mary Lou) Kaempfer of Surprise, Ariz. and West Bend; and nieces, nephews, other relatives and friends.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was preceded in death by his father Alfred Meyer and mother Catharine Meyer-Hazelwood.
2 CONT
2 CONT The family will greet relatives and friends during a period of visitation on Wednesday, April 17 at St. James Episcopal Church from 4-6 p.m. The Funeral Mass will be at 6 p.m. at the church with Masonic services to follow. Private
2 CONC  burial will be in Washington County Memorial Park.
2 CONT
2 CONT In lieu of flowers, the family has requested memorials to St. James Episcopal Church, the Washington County Historical Society or the West Bend Baseball Association.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Schmidt Funeral Home of West Bend is serving the family. Bob's family would like to extend a sincere thank you to Dr. Robert Gibson, Jeanine Schroeter, Dr. Sullivan, Amber, Amanda and the entire Lighthouse of West Bend staff f
2 CONC or being so caring and compassionate. Obituary contributed by Laura* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/130249080/robert-a_-meyer Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''O
2 CONC ct 15 2019, 0:25:20 UTC''
2 CONT
