2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services for Otto E. Shaw, 76, of Oconomowoc, Wis., will be held noon Monday, at Our Savior's Lutheran Church, 145 Lisbon Road, Oconomowoc, with the Rev. Mark Rydberg officiating. Born April 3, 1927, in Highland Park, he d
2 CONC ied Thursday, Aug. 21, 2003, at his residence. Burial will be in LaBelle Cemetery. Otto was a loss and prevention engineer for Schirmer Engineering in Illinois. He was a member of Our Savior's Lutheran Church, the Elks Club and th
2 CONC e American Legion Post in Arlington Heights. Otto was a graduate of Carthage College and was a World War II Army Air Corp, 9th Air Force Veteran. He was the husband Doris (nee Tarnow), who he married Feb. 14, 1953, in Chicago; fat
2 CONC her of Nancy (Thomas) Massnick of Oconomowoc and Neil W. (Janis) Shaw of Rochelle, Ill.; grandfather of seven; and brother of Robert (Joyce) Zschau of Matoon, Ill. Otto was preceded in death by his parents, Otto Zschau and Dorothy
2 CONC  Avery; and by one sister. Visitation will be held from 10 a.m. until! the time of services at noon Monday, at the church. Memorials may be made to Our Savior's Lutheran Church or the Oconomowoc Regional Cancer Center.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arrangements were made by Schmidt & Bartelt, Inc., Oconomowoc. Friends may visit www.dailyherald.com/obits to express condolences and sign the guest book. For funeral information, (262)567-4459.
2 CONT
