1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Died in Marshfield Township in Lincoln County, MN.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary's parents, Frederick and Mary Anna (Conrad) Jungers came to America in 1854 with their then 4 children and Frederick's brother Jacques. They sailed from Havre, France on the "Lamont" and arrived in New York on August 21, 1854
2 CONC . They began using the name Yungers around 1860-1870 and on the 1880 US Census for Belvidere, MN, they used the name Youngers. They lived in Belgium and Fredonia, Ozaukee County, WI around 1854 to 1960 and moved to Chester Townshi
2 CONC p, Wabasha County, MN before 1870. In 1880 they were in Belvidere, Goodhue County, MN.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=42043578
2 CONT
2 CONT AKA Mary Yungers
2 CONT
2 CONT Died in Marshfield Township in Lincoln County, MN.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary's parents, Frederick and Mary Anna (Conrad) Jungers came to America in 1854 with their then 4 children and Frederick's brother Jacques. They sailed from Havre, France on the "Lamont" and arrived in New York on August 21, 1854
2 CONC . They began using the name Yungers around 1860-1870 and on the 1880 US Census for Belvidere, MN, they used the name Youngers. They lived in Belgium and Fredonia, Ozaukee County, WI around 1854 to 1960 and moved to Chester Townshi
2 CONC p, Wabasha County, MN before 1870. In 1880 they were in Belvidere, Goodhue County, MN.
