1 NOTE {geni:about_me} OBITUARY (Winona Post 3/21/2007) Celestine S. Neeser, 92, of Wabasha and formerly of Lewiston, died Friday March 16, 2007, at St. Elizabeth's Hospital in Wabasha.
2 CONT
2 CONT Celestine was born January 26, 1915, in Tyler, MN, to Henry and Henrietta (Baasen) Prom. She married Leonard Neeser May 30, 1938, in Sauk Rapids, MN. They moved to Lewiston in 1958. Leonard died June 12, 1991. Celestine later ente
2 CONC red St. Elizabeth's Care Center in Wabasha. She was a homemaker and community volunteer.
2 CONT
2 CONT Celestine is survived by her children, Roger (Boni) Neeser of Stillwater, Dennis (Ruthanne) of Willmar and a daughter, Marian (Paolo) Romero of Fort Collins, Co. She is also survived by nine grandchildren, twelve great-grandchildr
2 CONC en, one great-great- grandchild, a brother, Ray St. Cloud and a sister Caroline of Sauk Rapids.
2 CONT
2 CONT A Funeral Mass will be 11AM Wednesday at St. Rose of Lima Catholic Church in Lewiston with the Reverends Marreddy Pothireddy and Milo Ernster concelebrating. Friends may call at the church from 9:30 AM Wednesday until time of serv
2 CONC ices. Hoff Funeral Home of Lewiston is assisting the family with arrangements. Please share a memory of Celestine at her on-line guestbook at www.hofffuneral.com.
2 CONT
2 CONT Memorials are preferred to the Luxembourg Heritage Museum, PO Box 63, Rollingstone, MN 55969.
