1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Harold J. Neeser, age 76, of Brainerd, passed away on Wed. June 15, 2005, at St. Joseph's Medical Center in Brainerd. Harold was born on Jan 31, 1929, in St. Cloud, Minn., to Theodore and Mary (Prom) Neeser. He was
2 CONC  raised in the Fort Ripley area and was united in marriage to Clara Mogensen on May 18, 1948, at St. Mathias Catholic Church in Fort Ripley.
2 CONT
2 CONT Over the years, Harold enjoyed vacationing in Branson, Mo. with his wife Clara, playing "500," watching western's, making home made ice cream and picnics. He also enjoyed his lake home on Hartley Lake and spending time with his fa
2 CONC mily. Harold was retired from Burlington Northern Railroad and was a member of St. Francis Catholic Church and the Moose Lodge in Brainerd.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is survived by two sons, John (Mary) Neeser of St. Paul and Tom (Diane) Neeser of Bemidji; three daughters, Cathy (Dave) Montour of Brooklyn Park; Cindy (Tom) Banker of Cottage Grove, and Marcy (Alan) Cunningham of Brainerd; 15
2 CONC  grandchildren, 10 great-grandchildren, and one brother, Dan (Vi) Neeser, of Fort Ripley.
2 CONT
2 CONT Harold was preceded in death by his parents, wife Clara, two daughters Mary and Liz, one son Peter, and one sister, Sister Marcelline.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mass of Christian Burial will be held on Tuesday, June 21 at 11 a.m. at St. Francis Catholic church in Brainerd with Father Seamus Walsh officiating. Interment will be in St. Mathias Cemetery, Fort Ripley. Friends may call on Mond
2 CONC ay from 5 - 8 p.m. with a rosary service at 7 p.m. at the Halvorson-Johnson Funeral Home in Brainerd and also at the church one hour prior to the service on Tuesday.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arrangements are with Halvorson-Johnson Funeral Home in Brainerd.
