1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/130466245/caroline-rone
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT OLDEST NATIVE RESIDENT DIES MRS. CAROLINE RONE, 86, LAST OF MELLEM FAMILY
2 CONT
2 CONT Northwood – Mrs. Caroline Rone, 88, the oldest native daughter of Worth County, died early Sunday morning in Northwood. She was the oldest daughter and last surviving member of a family of 12 children born to the late Gulbrand O. 
2 CONC and Karine Ellingson Mellem. Her parents were the first pioneer settlers of Worth County. Her brother, Ole G. Mellem had the distinction of being the first white child born in Worth County. Caroline Mellem was born near her presen
2 CONC t home May 19, 1857. She was baptized by the pioneer pastor, the Rev. C. L. Clausen, and confirmed by the late Rev. t. A. Torgerson.
2 CONT
2 CONT On May 18, 1882 she was united in marriage to Tollef C. Rone, who died January 18, 1935. To this union were born 5 children: Mrs. Brede Wamstad of Osage; Mrs. A. C. S. Rue of Des Moines; Mrs. Oliver Knutson of Northwood; Carl t. R
2 CONC one of Northwood and Mrs. L. H. Racker of Waverly, all of whom survive.
