1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=53216287
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=80298190
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=53208819
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Knute and Barbo came to American in 1858. They lived in Worth Co., IA until 1878 when they moved to Dakota. He settled first on the SE 1/4 sec 24, Newburgh Twp. 148, R 54, but later sold it to his son, Knute, and bought the SE 1/4
2 CONC  sec 17 in Newburgh Twp. which was railroad land. He donated one acre of this land for the site of Goose River Church.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://trees.ancestry.com/tree/32646281/person/18304098007
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Residence: 1860, Rural Spring Grove, Minnesota; south of Albert Lea, before moving to Iowa, then North Dakot.    According to SEVRE-SLEKT history, there is a fine book about Barbro and Knut (this needs research).
1 FAMS @F6000000031592903903@
1 RFN geni:6000000031592903898
1 SUBM @S6000000003887373302@
1 OBJE
2 FILE https://media.geni.com/p13/a7/6e/2c/bd/5344483d476cb24e/80298190_134955565111_original.jpg?hash=ad094bec7727871c9ed2ba126564bcf8af9207414be2d32ed0b27fcbb546e44e.1795161599
