2 FORM jpg
1 OBJE
2 FILE https://media.geni.com/p13/0d/a8/bb/14/5344483c065a633a/deh43cay_original.jpg?hash=323d716512a230113bba5253a6c9beb018057b1dd73fa864eac1743de5b75e67.1795161599
2 FORM jpg
1 NOTE
2 CONT November 28, 2005 - Ron Bestrom has confirmed some of this information with a link to the family burial site in Goose River Lutheran Church Cemetery.  Ron, who seems never to sleep, is digging further to fill in some gaps.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also Viggo Fosse came up with census information about this family, only his name now is Knut OSTENSON (his patronymic)
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1860, they are living in Highland Township, Winneshiek County, IA, across the border from Houston County, MN - about 10 miles apart.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1870, he is now Knut ASTENSON and they are living in Hartland Township, Worth County, IA
2 CONT
2 CONT (Viggo, I'd love to have a copy of the Dec 1884 photo y9u speak of in Fargp. ND)
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1880, I found that now Knud O. PLADSEN, and his family are living in District 68, Trail County. ND:  Knud - 50, Barbo - 49, Peter - 18, Knud O -17, Magrithe - 12, and Maria - 10.
2 CONT
2 CONT There appears to be TWO books of interest for me:  Marsha's reference to "The Pladson Family Book, 1966"  (Sevre-Slekt, p. 275)-+and Aagot Raaen's manuscripts, which Ron refers to: http://snipurl.com/kab0  In this list, I can see 
2 CONC several areas of interest to me.  So I'll need to contact NDSU.  Marsha, do you have a copy of the book you refer to?
2 CONT
2 CONT And Steinar Vissebraaten, your input on the PLADSON family ALSO is greatly appreciated.  I'm STILL trying to digest the Norwegian terms and fit the information into the right 'pockets'.-
2 CONT
2 CONT Th original search was for information regarding the death and location for Barbro Nilsdtr. LILLEGARD.  So far, we have no definite answer. Clark in Japan-  Clark & Mieko Pederson <araki-pederson@mtf.biglob.ne.jp
2 CONT
2 CONT Nov 25, 2005 - A brief history of the Goose River Lutheran Church appears on pg 23 in the Hatton Diamond Jubilee book (1959) and it lists the charter members: OSTEN H. PLADSON, KNUT O. PLADSON, P. K. PLADSON, KK. PLADSON, B. K. PL
2 CONC ADSON, ---(the last 3 are Knut's sons Peder, Knut and Bendik)  It goes on to say "KNUT O. PLADSON donated an acre of land for a very beautiful church site and in 1888 a church was built, but in 1889, before it was finished, a torn
2 CONC ado demolished it. Much of the lumber was salvaged and rebuilding was started in 1893. By 1898 it was completed at a total cost of $885 and was dedicated that same year by Pastor Gustaf OFTEDAHL.  Osten H. PLADSON,  a very capable
2 CONC  carpenter, supervised all the building and also made the altar, altar ring, pulpit and baptismal font."
2 CONT The Knut O. PLADSON bio (on page 75 in same book) says it was his son Knut who donated the land (in SE 1/4 of Section 17 in Newburgh Twp.)
2 CONT
2 CONT November 25, 2005 - Knut Ostensen Pladson and Barbro are my 2nd great-grand uncle and aunt.  I believe we are looking at the same migration patters for dozens and dozens of people from Nes to North Dakota--Clark & Mieko Pederson
2 CONT
2 CONT From Marsha Gunderson --Nov 26,2005 - Knut O. and Barbo Pladsen are my great, great, great grandparents.
