2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Bendick came to America in 1858 with his parents. The family settled at Worth Co., IA.  In 1878, he came to Dakota Territory and homesteaded on SE 1/4, sec 18 Newburgh Twp.
2 CONT
2 CONT ****************
2 CONT Last Name:  Pladson
2 CONT First Name:  Bendick
2 CONT Born:  1856
2 CONT Died:  1913
2 CONT Illustration:   ill.
2 CONT Publication: Hatton's Heritage: A History of Hatton, North Dakota, 1884-1959. [1959]
2 CONT Institute Call Number: F644.H38 H39
2 CONT Page No: 73
2 CONT
2 CONT Publication: Hatton Centennial, 1884-1984: A Century of Change. 1983.
2 CONT Institute Call Number: F644.H38 H38 1984
2 CONT Page No: 319
2 CONT
2 CONT *****************
2 CONT From Hatton Book:
2 CONT
2 CONT Bendick was born in Ness, Hallingdahl, Norway, in 1856,   He came to America with his parents in 1858.  The family settled at Worth County IA.  In 1878, he came to Dakota Territory and homesteaded...
2 CONT
2 CONT *********
2 CONT From: Grand Forks Herald, July 4, 1913
2 CONT "Think Groth May Recover"
2 CONT Iver Groth, who was severely injured in the automobile accident near Hatton, Wednesday...
2 CONT ...Mr. B. K. Pladson, who was killed in the accident by being smothered beneath the machine, was the brother of Miss Margaret Pladson of this city.  Miss Pladson has been employed as housekeeper at the Frederick Hotel for a number
2 CONC  of years.   She will attend the funeral which will be held from the home west of Hatton.
