1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Margaret Pladson Rites Held Friday, May 10th
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services were held last Friday afternoon, May 10th at 2 o’clock from the Goose River Lutheran Church for Margaret Pladson, who passed away at her home in Fargo Saturday, May 4th. Rev. K.C. Grundahl officiated and burial wa
2 CONC s in the churchyard cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Pladson was born May 7, 1868 near Northwood, Worth County, Iowa of parents Knudt O. Pladson and Barbo Pladson.   She came with her parents to North Dakota in 1877 and they settled in Newburgh township.   She had resided i
2 CONC n Newburgh all her life except the last 32 years when she had lived and worked in Fargo.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is survived by one brother, P.K. Pladson of Hatton, in addition to a large number of nieces and nephews and other relatives and friends who mourn her sudden passing.   She was preceded in death by her parents and nine brothers
2 CONC  and sisters. - Hatton Free Press, May 16, 1946
