1 NOTE
2 CONT Peter S. Evenson of Lansford passed away in the Trinity Hospital in Minot Tuesday morning at 7 o'clock.  Saturday about noon he was found lying unconscious in his farmhouse south of town, having suffered a paralytic stroke.  He wa
2 CONC s immediately rushed to the hospital in Minot where he died without regaining consciousness.
2 CONT Peter S. Evenson was born in Hallingdal, Norway on February 21, 1852. He immigrated to America in about 1860, settling in Iowa.  Later he moved to Spring Grove, Minnesota where he lived until 1888 when he came to Northwood, North 
2 CONC Dakota and took up a homestead.  In 1906 he came to Lansford and bought farm property south of town and lived here until his death.  A little over a year ago, he suffered a paralytic stroke from which he never fully recovered.  La
2 CONC st winter he spent at Hot Springs, Arkansas.  He returned here last May, apparently in better health, but became worse again.
2 CONT He leaves behind to mourn his loss, five brothers and one sister. They are:  Teman S. Evenson, Rushford, MN; Christian S. Evenson, Spring Grove; Ole S. Evenson, Bratsburg, Minnesota; Even S. Evenson, Ulen, Minnesota; Arne S. Evens
2 CONC on, Spokane, Washington; and Mrs. Kare Gullings, Mabel, Minnesota.
2 CONT His two brothers, Teman and Christ and a nephew, Edwin Evenson of Fargo arrived here last night to make arrangements for the funeral which will be held from the English Lutheran Church here at 2 o'clock tomorrow afternoon with the
2 CONC  Rev. Gable officiating.  Burial will be made here. Messages have been sent to his brothers and sister and some of them are expected here for the funeral.--The Lansford Leader
