1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Clara L. Neeser passed away Monday, Sept. 29, 2003, at Bethany Good Samaritan Village.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born March 25, 1928, in Brainerd to Fredrick and Betsy (Nesheim) Mogensen. She married Harold Neeser on May 18, 1948, in St. Mathias Township. She was a cook with 31 years at Kavanaugh's. She was a member of the Moose and 
2 CONC St. Francis Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survived by her husband, Harold; her sons, John of St. Paul, and Tom of Bemidji; her daughters, Cathy Montour of Brooklyn Park, Cindy Banker of Cottage Grove, and Marcy LaDouceur of Brainerd; her brother, Elmer of Orem, Utah; her 
2 CONC sister, Marie Satchell of Hugo; 15 grandchildren; and seven great-grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was preceded in death by two daughters, Mary and Liz, and one son, Peter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Services will be 11 a.m. Friday, Oct. 3, at St. Francis Catholic Church, Brainerd, with Father Seamus Walsh officiating. Friends may call from 5-8 p.m. Thursday, Oct. 2, at the funeral home and one hour prior to the service at the
2 CONC  church. Women of the Moose will have a memorial service at 6:30 p.m. Thursday at the funeral home. There will be a prayer service on Thursday at 7 p.m. at the funeral home.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arrangements are with Halvorson-Johnson Funeral Home, Brainerd.
