2 CONT Pg 165-66 of Gerhard Naeseth's book entitled "Norwegian Immigrants to U. S. 1847-48 - #920 - Kari Svensdtr. Eidal [Mary Knutson, 24, f] daughter of Svend Olsen Eidal and Kari Olsdtr., born March 29, 1813, died 1888. There were at 
2 CONC least ten children, including five born in Norway.  Kari m. Bendik Knudsen Thoen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 6 & 7 - History of the Storlie Family in America-- Bendick  was a brother to Knut Knutson (Thon) Storlie
2 CONT
2 CONT Pg 165 - Gerhard Naeseth's book Norwegian Immigrants to United States - 1847-48 - #919 "Bendick" Immigrated in 1848 aboard "Thracian " -arrived in New York Jul 31, 1848 from Gothenburg Sweden with 90 steerage passengers.  Captain 
2 CONC Richard Rogers. It was a  13 week voyage.  They came from Nes, Bu  to Plymouth Twp.,  Rock County via Milwaukee, WI.  Lived on farm SW of Hanover, Wisconsin (farm later owned by Torris Everson)
2 CONT
2 CONT Pg 165 - Bendik Knudsen Thoen [Bendik Knudson, 51, m] son of Knud Olsen Thoen and Margit, bp November 11, 1792, died 1861.  Emigrated from Nes, Buskerud to Plymouth Twp., Rock County, WI. Farmer. Married, October 22, 1835
2 CONT 920. Kari Svendsdtr. Eidal (Kary Knudson, 34 f], daughter of Svend Olsen Eidal and Kari Olsdtr., born March 29, 1913, died 1888.  There were at least ten children, including five born in Norway:
2 CONT 921 Margit Bendiksdtr. Thoen [Margaret Knudson, 12f] born March 7, 1836, died by 1850
2 CONT 922. Knud Bendiksen Thoen [Knude Knudson, 10 m], born October 11, 1838, died 1909.  Married, 1860-1867, Olene Pedersdtr Gaarder (1843:799) daughter of Peder Hovelsen Gaarder and Randine Olsdtr born in Nordre Land, Opland, November
2 CONC  12, 1840, died June 18 1867.  She had emigrated from Nordre Land, Opland in 1843.  Knud was married a second time, Guri born 1855, died 1924.  Knud and Guri arae buried in the Orfordville Lutheran Cemetery.
2 CONT 923. Kari Bendiksdtr. Thoen (Hary Knudson, 8 f] born June 7, 1841
2 CONT 924. Svend Bendiksen Thoen [Siver Knudson, 3, m] born August 1, 1845, died 1848 just as the ship landed in New York, buried in Milwaukee, WI.
2 CONT 925. Ole Bendiksen Thoen [Ole Knudson, 1m, m] born April 10, 1847, died March 16, 1917.  Moved about 1866 to Spring Grove, MN.  Served as Postmaster and later in the MN State legislature.
2 CONT 925 a. Mætte Christine Bendiksdtr Thoen, born July 24, 1848 on the passage to America.  Married Albert Olmstead.
2 CONT Children born in America to Bendik Knudsen Thoen and Kari Svensdtr. include Margith, born July 38, 1850; Oline born December 14, 1851; Karine, born March 2, 1853; Svend born 1857? -- Nes, Buskerud, Norway, Church records; 1860 WI 
2 CONC census; Luther Valley Lutheran Church records; Orfordville Lutheran Cemetery.
