1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT == Biography == 
2 CONT Jens was baptized 20 October 1793 at Nes i Hallingdal, the son of [[Myhre-89|Christian Myhre]] and  [[Kvie-5|Ragne Kvie]]. His godparents were Guro and Knud Myhre, Birgit Olsdatter, and Halvor and Ole Lane.<ref>[https://media.digi
2 CONC talarkivet.no/view/3050/58  Record of the Baptism]of Jens Christiansen Myhre. Baptized in the Church in 1793, Baptism number 174, at Nes, 21st Sunday after Trinity; 20th October, Jens, son of Christen and Ragne Myre. Witnesses: Gu
2 CONC ro and Knud Myhre, Birgit Olsdatter, Halvor and Ole Lane. Nes kirkebøker, F/Fa/L0005: Ministerialbok nr. 5, 1787-1807, s. 106-107.</ref> Jens was confirmed on 19 June 1814 at the age of 20.<ref>Den Norske kirke, Nesprestegjeld (Bu
2 CONC skerud),Kirkeboke., 1693-1925.</ref>
2 CONT Jens was a little bit of a rascal. In 1817, at the age of twenty-four, he had an illegitimate child with an unmarried girl, Kari Helgesdatter. Their son, Ole Jensen, was born 28 Sep 1817. Seven years later, on 10 January 1824, Jen
2 CONC s married a farmer's daughter, Elie Olsdatter Hova, in a double wedding with Elie's sister, Barbra. <ref>[https://media.digitalarkivet.no/view/3053/19584/1 Record of the Marriage] of Eli Olsdatter Høva and Jens Christiansen Myhre.
2 CONC  Nes kirkebøker, F/Fa/L0008: Ministerialbok nr. 8, 1824-1834, s. 690-691.</ref> After their marriage, Jens and Eli lived on the Myhre Farm.  She and Jens had four children: Ragne (1824-1906); Christen (1826-1907); Birgit (1830-191
2 CONC 9) and Ole (1833-1903). <ref>Gards-Og Slektshistorie ForNes i Hallingdal, Vol. IV, by Terje Østro, pages 356-357.</ref> Jens's father, Christian, died ten years after the double wedding. In 1810, Jens borrowed 800 rdlr. of the Osl
2 CONC o Cathedral Cathedral, against a mortgage in the farm that was valued for 2000 rdlr. <ref>Gards-Og Slektshistorie For Nes i Hallingdal, Vol. IV, by Terje Østro, pages356-357.</ref> In 1827, Jens gave a payment for the legacy of hi
2 CONC s sister Eli Kristensdatter married to Anfinn gutterormsen in Hedalen and his sister Unn Kristensdatter married Knut Bjørnsen in Skoger; each sister received 47sp. a total of 94 spdlr.<ref>Gards-Og Slektshistorie For Nes i Halling
2 CONC dal, Vol. IV, by Terje Østro, pages 356-357.</ref> Jens purchased the family farm from his father in 1823, a year before his marriage. Jens was listed as the owner and farmer at Myhre Nordre in the 1838 land register. In 1849, Jen
2 CONC s sold half of the farm to his son, Christen, for 200 spdlr and Jens continued to live there until his death a year later.<ref>Gards-Og Slektshistorie For Nes i Hallingdal, Vol. IV, by Terje Østro, pages 356-357.</ref> In 1849 the
2 CONC  farm was described at the time Jens sold it to his son. The farm had two cows and six small farm animals. It produced three bushels of rye and three bushels of mixed grains. One half of the farm wasdevoted to growing crops and th
2 CONC e other part forest. There was also a green house. Jens did not live a long life and died at the age of fifty-seven on 19October 1850.<ref>[https://media.digitalarkivet.no/view/1110/590  Record of the Death and Burial] of Jens Chr
2 CONC istiansen Myhre. Nes kirkebøker, F/Fa/L0009: Ministerialbok nr. 9, 1834-1863, s. 547.</ref> Jens's estate was settled on 2 December 1850.  In 1850, Jens half the garden to his son Kristen for 200 spdlr. And in1850, Jens sold the o
2 CONC ther half to Erick Svensen Myhre for 200 spdlr. but with the exception of the outbuilding and the house.  Then it saysthat there were Saupeset and Lisleset, some of whom have something togo here and England, half of the Myreremmen
2 CONC  and the farm called Høveremmen. So the farm was divided at this time.<ref>Gards-Og Slektshistorie For Nes i Hallingdal, Vol. IV, by Terje Østro, pages 356-357.</ref> His wife, Elie, lived another fifteen years, remaining on the M
2 CONC yhre farm. She died there at the age of seventy. After Jens's death, his son,Christen, took over the Myhre farm. Jens's illegitimate son, Ole, moved to Aal at Hallingdal, where he lived at the farm Kanafet-Myro. Ole was a fiddler.
2 CONC   His wife's name was Kirsti Syverdatter Sundre. Ole died at Aal in 1904 at the age of eighty-seven. One of his sons, Nub Olsen Myre, emigrated to North Dakota, where he was married and had eleven children. Nub died in 1948 at Cli
2 CONC fford, North Dakota.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
