2 CONT Plot: In same lot as Alfred & Marion (Frydenlund) Lunde
2 CONT
2 CONT http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~knorthup/Webpage/Atlanta/Lunde/LundeHTMpages/OlePLundeFamily.htm Margaret Emilia Lunde was born September 21, 1883 in Thief River Falls, Minnesota. She is the only child of Ole & Ingeborg L
2 CONC unde who was not born in Hayward, Freeborn Co., Minnesota, and they lived in Freeborn County all of their married life. I believe that Margaret was born in Thief River because Ingeborg Lunde traveled up to northern Minnesota to at
2 CONC tend the wedding of her sister Caroline Viker to O. M. Omlie on August 27, 1883 in Fargo, North Dakota; it is my guess that she then stayed with her parents who were living near Thief River Falls until Margaret was born before tra
2 CONC veling home again. She is listed as Margith, age 11, with her parents on the 1895 census of Hayward, Freeborn, Minnesota. The family moved from Hayward to Moscow, Minnesota sometime between 1895-1900, and Margaret is listed with h
2 CONC er parents on the 1900, 1905, & 1910 censuses of Moscow, Freeborn Co., Minnesota. Margaret never married. I have not found her on the 1920 census at this time, but her parents retired from farming that year and moved into Hayward,
2 CONC  Freeborn Co., Minnesota. Margaret is listed with them on the 1930 census Hayward Village, Freeborn Co., Minnesota. Her father Ole died in 1933, and Margaret is listed at age 56 with her mother and two female boarders on the 1940 
2 CONC census of Hayward, Freeborn, Minnesota. Margaret was an excellent seamstress and made many of her sisters and cousins dresses. Margaret Lunde died on May 7, 1982 in Albert Lea, Freeborn Co., Minnesota. 
