1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gladys Borgen, 96  Print	 E-mail	 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Written by TRF Times      
2 CONT   Thief River Falls - Gladys Borgen, 96, died Wednesday, May 30, 2007 at Northwest Medical Center, Thief River Falls.
2 CONT    Funeral services were held on Sunday, June 3, at Johnson Funeral Service, Thief River Falls, with Rich Raschke officiating.  Interment was held at Greenwood Cemetery, Thief River Falls.
2 CONT       Gladys Marie Syversrud was born February 1, 1911 in Pennington  County, the daughter of Knute and Andrea Elizabeth (Evenvik) Syversrud. She attended school in the Highlanding area.
2 CONT       As a young lady, Gladys took care of her mother and also did domestic work in the McIntosh area. In 1940, she moved to Thief River Falls and became employed in the Hartz Bakery. She worked for Hartz Wholesale for 10 years, r
2 CONC etiring at the age of 70.
2 CONT       On June 2, 1949, Gladys was united in marriage to Harold Borgen in Thief River  Falls. The couple made their home at 124 State St. N. in Thief River Falls, where she was a home maker. She lived there until moving into Greenl
2 CONC eaf Assisted Living, Thief  River Falls in 2005.
2 CONT       Gladys enjoyed crocheting and visiting with family and friends.
2 CONT       She is survived by a daughter, Beverly (Joseph) Anderson of Buffalo; and a grandson.
2 CONT       Gladys was preceded in death by husband, Harold in 1957; parents; brothers and sisters, Synneva Swenson, Ned Syversrud, Edwin Syversrud, Christine Vidden, Martha Tollefson, Ned Syversrud, Carl Syversrud, Gena Van Keuren, Ado
2 CONC lph Syversrud and Ruth Mosbeck.    A00003B2007JN06  
