1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Hatton Pioneer Laid to Rest
2 CONT Funeral services were held at the Goose River Church last Thursday, March 30, for Mrs. Bendick Pladson, 89 (nee Andrine Kittelson), a resident of Newburgh township for 57 years. She passed away at the Northwood Old Peoples Home on
2 CONC  Friday evening, March 24, where she had stayed after a fall which injured her hip.
2 CONT Rev. A.E. Setness officiated at the services. Miss Quanrud of Northwood sang two selections with Mrs. H.G. Wambheim at the organ.
2 CONT Pallbearers were six grandsons: Graydon Pladson, James Pladson, Olaf Midtbo, Lloyd Pladson, Reuben Sondreaal and Edward Pladson.
2 CONT Mrs. Pladson was born Nov. 11, 1860 in Freeborn County near Albert Lea, Minn. of parents Kjetil and Veel Kittelson. Here her father died and was buried. A few years later her mother remarried and the family came to Dakota Territor
2 CONC y in the early eighties.
2 CONT After her marriage to Bendick Pladson on March 17, 1893, she was a member of the Goose River congregation and Goose River Ladies Aid, living on the old homestead six miles west of Hatton. Her husband passed away in 1913.
2 CONT Those surviving are Mrs. M.E. [Malvine] Sondreaal, Mrs. Tollef [Angela] Midtbo, Willie and Ostinius Pladson and Mrs. Peder [Florence] Bjerke, all of Hatton; Clifford Pladson of Milwaukee, Wis., Mrs. Ella Barton of Beechy, Sask., C
2 CONC anada.  Also two step-children, Nickolai Pladson of Northwood and Mrs. Charles Wichert of Fertile, Minn.   She also leaves 19 grandchildren and 5 great-grandchildren.
2 CONT Besides her immediate family, she leaves one half-sister, Mrs.
2 CONT Isabelle Storkson of Glasgow, Mont., two half-brothers, Lauritz Christopher
2 CONT of Emerado and William Christopher of Grand Forks.
2 CONT Other relatives and friends here for the funeral included Mrs.
2 CONT William Christopher, Arnold and Emmons, Mrs. Tilda Christopher, Arthur
2 CONT Christopher, Mrs. Herbert Tinnes, Mrs. Merton Hiestand, Mrs. Julia Nelson,
2 CONT Bert Nelson, Mr. and Mrs. Geo. Brunsvold and Mrs. Oliver Bjerke and Fay,
2 CONT all of Grand Forks, Mr. and Mrs. Joe Sparrow and Mae Sparrow of Clifford
2 CONT and Mrs. Robert Brown of Fargo. - Hatton Free Press, April 6, 1950
