2 CONT Florence Bjerke, 87 Passed Away
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services were held for Florence Bjerke, 87 of Hatton on Monday, October 7, 1991 at 10:30 a.m. in the Goose River Lutheran Church, rural Hatton. She died Friday [Oct. 4] at the Tri-County Nursing Home in Hatton. She was bor
2 CONC n on June 3, 1904 in Newburgh Township, rural Hatton, the daughter of the late Bendick Pladson and Annie Kittleson. She attended rural school in Newburgh Township, high school in Newburgh Township and college at Mayville. She taug
2 CONC ht rural school in Beaver Creek Township, rural Hatton prior to her marriage to Peder O. Bjerke on March 15, 1927 at Hatton. The couple farmed in Newburgh Township west of Hatton until their retirement in 1969 when they moved into
2 CONC  Hatton to live. He died December 24, 1977. She became a resident at the Tri-County Nursing Home in May of 1983. She was a lifelong member of the Goose River Lutheran Church and its WELCA. She is survived by her sons Philip of St.
2 CONC  Paul, MN and Bendick of Atlanta, CA and four grandchildren. She was preceded in death by four brothers, Nickolae, Ostinius, Willie and Clifford and five sisters, Mrs. Sam (Ella) Barton, Mrs. Charles (Beata) Wichert, Mrs. Ed (Caro
2 CONC lyn) Sparrow, Mrs. M.E. (Malvina) Sondreaal and Mrs. Tollef (Angela) Midtbo. Services were held Monday, Oct. 7 at 10:30 a.m. at the Goose River Lutheran Church, rural Hatton with Pastor Duane Neugebauer officiating. The organist w
2 CONC as Ada Thompson and Eunice and Renae Grimson sang a duet. Casketbearers were Myron Sondreaal, Olaf Midtbo, Guy Midtbo, Edward Pladson, James Pladson, Russell Pladson, Ray Pladson, Lloyd Pladson, and Graydon Pladson. The interment 
2 CONC was held in the Goose River Cemetery. The Bilden-Arnett Funeral Home was in charge of the arrangements. -- Hatton Free Press, Oct. 1991
2 CONT
