2 CONT Nickolai Pladson, Northwood, Dies August 21 in Hospital
2 CONT
2 CONT Nickolai B. Pladson was born July 17, 1884 in Newburgh Township near Hatton. His parents were the late Bendick and Gurie (Mehus) Pladson.   He was baptized and confirmed at Goose River Lutheran Church and attended school near his 
2 CONC parental home and later Bruflat Academy, Portland, N.D.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Esther Bratrud in 1910 at Grand Forks.   They homesteaded in South Dakota and came back to the Hatton community in 1912 and farmed in Newburgh Township until 1932.   They lived on the farm until 1948 when they moved to 
2 CONC Northwood to live.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Pladson died February 8, 1962. He had been a resident at the Northwood Nursing Home since 1969 and died at the Northwood Hospital August 21 [1973].
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are four sons; Bendick and Abner of Northwood, Leonard and Kermit of Grand Forks and six grandchildren as well as the following brothers and sisters: Willie Pladson, Hatton, Clifford Pladson, Milwaukee, Mrs. M. E. (Malvi
2 CONC na) Sondreal, Mrs. Tollef (Angela) Midtbo and Mrs. Peder (Florence) Bjerke all of Hatton.   He was preceded in death by his wife and two sons, Guy and Amos.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services were held August 24 at Swarstad Chapel, Northwood, with Rev. Julian Erickson and Rev. John Johanson officiating. Burial was in Goose River Cemetery. Organist was Mrs. Hannah Haga and soloist was Steven Kordahl.
2 CONT
2 CONT Casketbearers were: Rueben Sondreal, Olaf Midtbo, Edward Pladson, Joseph Sparrow, Lloyd Pladson and James Pladson, nephews of Nickolai. Arnett Funeral Home, Northwood, had charge of arrangements. - Hatton Free Press, Aug. 30, 1973
2 CONT
