1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Margaret Pladson Died at Her Home Here Yesterday
2 CONT
2 CONT Miss Margaret Pladson, daughter of P.K. Pladson of Hatton died at her home here late yesterday [July 19, 1933] afternoon.   She was born at Hatton March 26, 1902.
2 CONT
2 CONT Deceased is survived by her father and five sisters and five brothers.  They are Mrs. George [Bella] Helland of Stanley, N.Dak., Mrs. Ernest [Esther] Pabst of St. Paul, Minnesota, Mrs. John Klanowskie of Denver, Colorado, Mrs. Edd
2 CONC ie [Mae] Von Rueden of Park River, N.Dak., Mrs. Roy [Elise] Flaten of Mayville, N.Dak., Alfred Pladson of Nashua, Montana, Carl Pladson of Binscarth, Manitoba, Canada, Edgar, Oliver and Gilbert Pladson, all of Hatton.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held Saturday afternoon at 2 o’clock from the Goose River Church with Rev. A.J. Eikeland in charge. - Hatton Free Press, July 20, 1933.
