2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT E. G. Brunsvold, Hatton Pioneer, Laid to Rest
2 CONT Funeral services for Mr. Erick G. Brunsvold, pioneer resident of this community, were held Saturday afternoon, February 8, from the Goose
2 CONT River Lutheran Church with Rev. C.J. Field officiating. Mrs. T.J. Thompson was organist and vocalists were Mrs. Alfred S. Thompson, Mrs. Peder Bjerke and Mrs. G.L. Thompson.
2 CONT Honorary pallbearers were Oscar O. Berg, Tollef Midtbo, Nick B. Pladson, G.O. Thompson, Sever O. Pladson, Dr. A.A. Kjelland, Nels Maystad,
2 CONT Sam K. Pladson, John L. Thompson and Benjamin Pladson.   Active pallbearers were Earl Brunsvold, Ray Brunsvold, Ervin Brunsvold, Duane Brunsvold, Oliver Bjerke and Rev. Johnson.   Burial was made in the Goose River
2 CONT cemetery. Olson, Hegg & Pederson Funeral Home were in charge of the arrangements.
2 CONT Mr. Brunsvold was born May 7, 1866 at Highlandville, Winneshiek
2 CONT County, Iowa, of parents Jorgen Olson Brunsvold and Barbo Guri Anesdotter
2 CONT Brunsvold.   At the age of 19 he came to North Dakota.   In 1891 he was married to Maria Pladson and they settled on a farm five miles west of Hatton.   To this union four boys were born, George, Bennie, Earle and Arthur.
2 CONT In 1909 Mrs. Brunsvold passed away. Mr. Brunsvold continued to live and work on the farm and raise his four sons.   He retired from active farming in 1942 and moved to Hatton.   In December of last year, he entered the Northwood O
2 CONC ld Peoples Home.   On the first of February 1958 he was taken  ill and entered the Northwood Hospital where he passed away February 6th.
2 CONT He is survived by his four sons, George of Grand Forks, Bennie of Mayville, Earle of Glen Lake, Minn. and Arthur of Chicago.   He also leaves
2 CONT 10 grandchildren and 28 great-grandchildren. He was preceded in death by his parents, three brothers, Ole, Arne and Jorgen, and two sisters, Brynil and Barbo. – Hatton Free Press, Feb. 13, 1958
