2 CONT
2 CONT                                                                       George C. Brunsvold
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth:  May 22, 1893 Hatton Traill County North Dakota, USA  Death:  Jul. 4, 1959 Grand Forks Grand Forks County North Dakota, USA 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hold Rites for Mr. George Brunsvold
2 CONT
2 CONT  George Brunsvold of Grand Forks, former resident of this community, passed away at his home in that city Saturday. Services were held Tuesday morning in the Hanson-Anderson Funeral Chapel in Grand Forks with Rev. R.S. Aanestad of
2 CONC ficiating.
2 CONT  A second service was held Wednesday afternoon at the Goose River Church near Hatton with Rev. C.J. Field officiating. Burial was made in the church cemetery.
2 CONT  Active pallbearers were Arnold Bye, Andrew, Kermit, Grayden and Joel Pladson, and Reuben Sondreaal. Honorary pallbearers were Olaf Bye, O.E. Green, Clarence Sanda, Allen Eide, Olaf Berg, Harry Hanson, Val Anderson, Leonard Rydell
2 CONC  and Willie, Sam and O.B. Pladson.
2 CONT  Mr. Brunsvold was born in Hatton May 22, 1893 and was married to Clara G. Berg on June 29, 1916. They lived in Hatton until 1947 when they moved to Grand Forks. Mr. Brunsvold has been associated with the Rydell Motor Co. at Grand
2 CONC  Forks.
2 CONT  Survivors include his wife; a daughter, Mrs. Oliver N. (Marie) Bjerke of Grand Forks; three sons, Ray of Hatton, and Earl and Duane of Minneapolis; three brothers, Ben of Mayville, Earle of Minneapolis and Arthur of Chicago, and 
2 CONC eight grandchildren. – Hatton Free Press, July 9, 1959 
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Goose River Lutheran Cemetery  Steele County North Dakota, USA 
2 CONT
2 CONT Created by: lk51t Record added: Jun 03, 2010  Find A Grave Memorial# 53215557 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
