2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Ben Brunsvold Dies Saturday
2 CONT
2 CONT Ben Brunsvold, 79, a resident of Mayville died Saturday July 6 in Luther Memorial Home, Mayville. Ben was born June 4, 1895 at Hatton to Mr. and Mrs. Erick Brunsvold. He grew to manhood at Hatton and married Olga Eide November 11,
2 CONC  1915 at Hatton. They farmed west of Hatton for 25 years. Later they owned and operated the Northern Hotel at Mayville for 19 years, retiring in 1972.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are his wife Olga at Mayville and a son and two daughters, Ervin Brunsvold, auditor with Atwood Larson at Minneapolis; Mrs. Carl (Grace) Bauer of State College, Pennsylvania and Mrs. Reynold (Beulah) Johnson of LeSueur, 
2 CONC Minn.   Also surviving are 16 grandchildren and 14 great-grandchildren. He was preceded in death by three brothers, George, Earl and Arthur Brunsvold.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services were held Tuesday July 9 at 2 o’clock at Goose River Lutheran Church, rural Hatton. Pastors Julian Erickson and Randall Paulson officiated. Burial was in Goose River Cemetery. Organist was Mrs. T.J. Thompson with 
2 CONC Donald Kvernen soloist.
2 CONT Casketbearers were Arlen Brunsvold, Ben E. Brunsvold, Robert Brunsvold, David Brunsvold, Ron Johnson, Tim Johnson and Mark Johnson. Baker Funeral Home, Mayville had charge of arrangements - Hatton Free Press, July 11, 1974
