2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Services Held for Arthur Brunsvold
2 CONT
2 CONT Arthur O. Brunsvold, former Hatton resident, passed away on January 20 in a Chicago hospital.   Funeral services were held Saturday afternoon, Jan. 23 at 2 o’clock at the Goose River Lutheran Church with Rev. C.J. Field officiatin
2 CONC g.   Burial was made in the Goose River cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pallbearers were Joel Pladson, James Pladson, Olaf Midtbo, Roland Pladson, NoBell Pladson and Andrew Pladson. Mrs. Gordon Pladson was soloist and Mrs. T.J. Thompson, organist.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Brunsvold was born near Hatton, Dec. 3, 1904, youngest son of the late Mr. and Mrs. Erick Brunsvold.   He attended school in Newburgh township, the Hatton High School and Concordia College, Moorhead, Minn.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1925 he left this community, first going to Milwaukee and then to Chicago.   For the past 15 years he had been employed by the New York Central Railroad in Chicago.
2 CONT He is survived by his wife and two brothers, Ben of Mayville and Earle of Glen Lake, Minn. Another brother, George, passed away last July.
2 CONT
2 CONT Olson, Hegg & Pederson Funeral Home were in charge of the arrangements. – Hatton Free Press, Jan. 28, 1960
