1 NOTE He came with his parents to Sheyenne in July, 1883 by covered wagon and settled on a farm about 1 1/2 miles southwest of Sheyenne.  Here he grew to manhood and took a homestead in Grandfield township and also purchased another qua
2 CONC rter section of land.
1 NOTE After their marriage a large reception was held at the Ole Hendrickson home with many guests present.  They then settled on their farm in a claim shanty.  The following year, in 1900 a new house was built and in 1910 an addition w
2 CONC as added on to it.  Mr. Hendrickson beautified his homestead by planting many trees and had a large grove with many evergreens.    He served on the school board, the township board and as a trustee for his church congregation.  Mr
2 CONC . and Mrs. Hendrickson were members of the Grandfield Luthean Church.  Mrs. Hendrickson was a charter member of the Ladies Aid.  In 1949 they celebrated their Golden Wedding Anniversary.
